      },
      "displayName": "Situ, Longshou",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=5d556d41400d9d0d9f53def0",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": {
      "content": [
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "attrs": {
           "accessLevel": "",
           "id": "60785ded115da6006f540529",
           "text": "@Andrew Woods"
          },
          "type": "mention"
         },
         {
          "text": " It looks like there's an character escaping issue with URI that contains the character colon ( : ), which is used as delimiter in jetty-users.properties (userName: password,userRole). I always got status 401 in the integration test suite org.fcrepo.integration.FedoraHtmlResponsesIT (fcrepo-webapp). What I'd tried including escape special character colon ( : ) with backslash(\\:, ",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": ": etc), URL escaping(%3A), unique code escaping (\\u003A, 0x3A etc) etc, hoping that Java can interpret it, but I have no luck.",
          "type": "text"
         },
         {
          "type": "hardBreak"
         },
         {
          "text": "However it works when I use the URL escaped version of : (%3A) in user URI and the escaped version as credential to login Fedora. But we may need to unescaped it before using the user URI in this case.",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       },
       {
        "content": [
         {
          "text": "Do you have any thoughts / suggestions to deal with it? Thanks.",
          "type": "text"
         }
        ],
        "type": "paragraph"
       }
      ],
      "type": "doc",
      "version": 1
     },
