       "24x24": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/9c216fdd7cb93a81bea8fb9ffc640f8e?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FSL-3.png",
       "32x32": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/9c216fdd7cb93a81bea8fb9ffc640f8e?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FSL-3.png",
       "48x48": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/9c216fdd7cb93a81bea8fb9ffc640f8e?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FSL-3.png"
      },
      "displayName": "Situ, Longshou",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=5d556d41400d9d0d9f53def0",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": "<p><a href=\"https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=60785ded115da6006f540529\" class=\"user-hover\" rel=\"60785ded115da6006f540529\" data-account-id=\"60785ded115da6006f540529\" accountid=\"60785ded115da6006f540529\" rel=\"noreferrer\">Andrew Woods</a> It looks like there's an character escaping issue with URI that contains the character colon ( : ), which is used as delimiter in jetty-users.properties (userName: password,userRole). I always got status 401 in the integration test suite org.fcrepo.integration.FedoraHtmlResponsesIT (fcrepo-webapp). What I'd tried including escape special character colon ( : ) with backslash(\\:, <br/>\n: etc), URL escaping(%3A), unique code escaping (\\u003A, 0x3A etc) etc, hoping that Java can interpret it, but I have no luck.<br/>\n However it works when I use the URL escaped version of : (%3A) in user URI and the escaped version as credential to login Fedora. But we may need to unescaped it before using the user URI in this case.</p>\n\n<p>Do you have any thoughts / suggestions to deal with it? Thanks.</p>",
     "created": "04/Oct/17 9:50 PM",
     "id": "19454",
     "jsdPublic": true,
     "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/issue/12538/comment/19454",
